\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Controlled contrasts. (a) MT-Bench: the same question set judged by expert humans (filled circles) and by GPT-4 (open squares). Values are $\hat  {k}/n$ in percent, with counts annotated. The GPT-4 leader needs a larger share of its data to change for top-1, but a smaller one for the top-3 set. (b) Fragility rank of the drop/top-1 cases by count (left, with $\hat  {k}$) and by fraction (right, with $\hat  {k}/n$). Rank 1 (top) is the most fragile. The ordering of Arena and the NBA seasons reverses between scales (purple).}}{8}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:contrasts}{{3}{8}{Controlled contrasts. (a) MT-Bench: the same question set judged by expert humans (filled circles) and by GPT-4 (open squares). Values are $\kver /n$ in percent, with counts annotated. The GPT-4 leader needs a larger share of its data to change for top-1, but a smaller one for the top-3 set. (b) Fragility rank of the drop/top-1 cases by count (left, with $\kver $) and by fraction (right, with $\kver /n$). Rank 1 (top) is the most fragile. The ordering of Arena and the NBA seasons reverses between scales (purple)}{figure.caption.23}{}}
